From 5ed421afb4d568a5f6047985cae3e63231d14364 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 05:06:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sycl: the MMVQ launchers declared one pair of ranges and
 launched with another

Eleven reorder_mul_mat_vec_*_sycl[_ncols] launchers in ggml-sycl/mmvq.cpp
declared `global_size` / `workgroup_size` (the q6_k one declared neither) and
then launched with `sycl::nd_range<3>(block_nums * block_dims, block_dims)`,
names that do not exist in those functions. The SYCL tree could not compile.
Not a b10819 artefact: `git log -S"256 / WARP_SIZE"` puts the declaration hunk
in patch 4-other-backends/0006-laguna-... (2026-08-15), and the pre-b10819 fork
at 95c1b6e69 already carried the mismatch. Neither the line-drop scan (nothing
upstream added is missing) nor the symbol scan (every name still occurs in the
file) can see this class; r17b_undeclared_scan.py in the lane evidence is the
scan that does.

Union, not a revert: upstream's launch shape (block_nums = workgroups,
block_dims = one workgroup) with the fork's mechanism kept inside it -
num_subgroups = 256 / WARP_SIZE, so a workgroup is 256 threads at either
subgroup width and stays under the Intel Arc Pro B70 512-thread limit that
upstream's num_subgroups = WARP_SIZE (1024 at WARP_SIZE 32) exceeds. The grid is
the one the fork's global_size described: ceil_div(nrows, MMV_Y*nsg) workgroups
of nsg*WARP_SIZE threads. The four launchers upstream left at WARP_SIZE are
untouched. R15B row 17 (Q4_K rows_per_sg, 4aa6ffba2) is present and unaffected.

NOT VERIFIED here: no SYCL toolchain on this estate. Union-by-mechanism-read;
compile verification is PENDING the first run of the sycl-ubuntu job.

Origin: ArifiLabs patch 4-other-backends/0006-laguna (B70 workgroup cap) unioned onto upstream llama.cpp b10819 (6a1a922d2) launch geometry
WI: WI-1702
Lane: lane-210
